      "outputTokens": 679,
      "costUsd": 0.0061595,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with saving instead of borrowing: two hundred dollars into an account at the end of every month, towards a first apartment, and the balance climbs. Now put a second account beside it. A hundred thousand dollars sits in a fund, and one thousand and fifty dollars ninety-one comes out at the end of every month, so the balance falls. One grows and one shrinks, but they're the same kind of thing. What do these two have in common?"
    },
