      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 109,
      "outputTokens": 796,
      "costUsd": 0.0072185,
      "pronunciationText": "An annuity is a run of equal payments made at regular times, with interest compounding on the balance every period. Compounding means the interest is added to the balance, so next period it earns interest too. There are two kinds. In the first, you make equal contributions into an investment account, and interest is added at the end of each period. In the second, you invest one single sum, then make equal withdrawals from it. Same size, same gap, the same rate each period. That's the pattern to look for."
    },
