      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 826,
      "costUsd": 0.007495,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's test the idea. Two thousand dollars invested once and left to grow. Is that an annuity? Make a guess. It isn't. It earns compound interest, but there are no regular payments, so it's just compound interest, like the growth models in the sequences videos. Deposits of fifty, then eighty, then a hundred and ten dollars a month aren't equal, so that's not an annuity either. And putting money in whenever you have spare cash isn't regular. But two hundred dollars at the end of every quarter, with interest each quarter, is."
    },
