      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 97,
      "outputTokens": 727,
      "costUsd": 0.0065915,
      "pronunciationText": "A cash-flow diagram shows the same thing on a time line. Time zero is when the account opens, and nothing goes in yet. Each arrow is one deposit, at the end of a period: at one, two, three, and so on, up to n. So n periods give n deposits. The future value is the balance at the end, at time n, straight after the last deposit. That last deposit has had no time to earn any interest yet."
    },
