      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 132,
      "outputTokens": 910,
      "costUsd": 0.008256,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the fund. A hundred thousand dollars earns four point eight per cent a year, compounded monthly, so the rate per month is zero point zero zero four. In the first month it earns four hundred dollars interest. Then the withdrawal of one thousand and fifty dollars ninety-one comes out, leaving ninety-nine thousand, three hundred and forty-nine dollars and nine cents. Here's the rule. The next balance is one plus r, times this balance, minus M. That's exactly the loan rule. A loan has the same cash flows, seen from the lender's side. One sum goes out, and equal amounts come back."
    },
