      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 123,
      "outputTokens": 810,
      "costUsd": 0.0073514999999999995,
      "pronunciationText": "Why does the fund run down? Each month the withdrawal is bigger than the interest, so the balance drops, and next month there's less to earn interest on. So it falls slowly at first, then faster, and runs out at the hundred and twentieth withdrawal, which is ten years. That last one is a little smaller, because the withdrawal is rounded up to the cent. If you only took out four hundred dollars, exactly the interest, the balance would stay at a hundred thousand forever. The withdrawal was set, the same way a loan repayment is set, so that the fund lasts ten years."
    },
