      "outputTokens": 745,
      "costUsd": 0.006758,
      "pronunciationText": "One more condition. In this course, interest compounds as often as the payments are made, so the rate and the count match the payments. Five hundred dollars a month for two years, at six per cent a year compounded monthly, has r equal to zero point zero zero five per month, and n equal to twenty-four months, not two. For quarterly payments, divide the annual rate by four. For fortnightly, divide by twenty-six. In this course, every payment comes at the end of its period."
