      "pronunciationText": "B and D are annuities. B has equal deposits every fortnight, with interest each fortnight. D starts with one sum and makes equal yearly withdrawals, with interest each year. C isn't, because the deposits aren't equal. Choosing ay is the classic mistake. It earns compound interest, but compound interest alone isn't an annuity. There are no regular payments."
